			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:32:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				44,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Worker): Add architectural flow diagram for caching and CSS interception\n\nExtend the Architecture.md documentation with a comprehensive Mermaid graph visualizing the Service Worker's internal structure and interaction model. The diagram details the multi-tier caching strategy (CACHE_CORE, CACHE_ASSET, CACHE_EXT), the custom CSS import interception mechanism via the CSS proxy module, and the registration flow initiated by the Sky UI layer.\n\nThis addition provides a clear visual reference for the network-to-cache routing logic, policy enforcement points, and telemetry bridge integration, complementing the existing textual description of the offline support architecture.",
			"SHA": "616c5b7677fac8ba1f52b3f012c30290b93c311c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:24:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				44,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Worker): Introduce architecture documentation for Service Worker\n\nCreate `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to provide a comprehensive technical overview of the Worker service worker implementation. This document details the multi-tier caching strategy (Network-first for core assets, Cache-first for static resources), the custom dynamic CSS loading mechanism using import interception, and the full service worker lifecycle from installation to activation.\n\nThe guide includes module maps, flow diagrams for the two-phase CSS loading strategy, and integration points with the Sky UI layer, serving as the definitive reference for the editor's offline support and asset delivery logic.",
			"SHA": "dd8cb34a599d3f2993f8a4545eb8844beac9e52a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
